title: qnnpack's quantized-add gives wrong result
github_labels: oncall: quantization|triaged|oncall: mobile
body_excerpt: ## 🐛 Bug qadd two qint8 tensor with qnnpack backend gives the wrong result in some condition. I have compared the result with fbgemm backend. This bug might caused by rounding. ## To Reproduce ```python import torch import struct def make_quint8_tensor(qint, scale, zero_point): return torch.quantize_per_tensor( torch.Tensor([(qint - zero_point) * scale]).to(torch.float32), scale=scale, zero_point=zero_point, dtype=torch.quint8, ) def print_qtensor(t): print( f'	quantized={t.int_repr().tolist()[0]}
' f'	float={t.dequantize()[0].item()}
' f'	scale={t.q_scale()}
' f'	zero_point={t.q_zero_point()}
' ) def set_backend(backend): torch.backends.quantized.engine = backend a_scale = struct.unpack('f', b'\xf1$&=')[0] # ~0.040562573820352554 b_scale = struct.unpack('f', b'.\xe5\xb5=')[0] # ~0.08881603181362152 c_scale = struct.unpack('f', b'L\xed\xb8=')[0] # ~0.09029635787010193 az, bz, cz = 112, 126, 124 aq = make_quint8_tensor(158, a_scale, az) bq = make_quint8_tensor(136, b_scale, bz) print('quint8 tensor a:') print_qtensor(aq) print('quint8 tensor b:') print_qtensor(bq) set_backend('fbgemm') cq = torch.ops.quantized.add(aq, bq, c_scale, cz) print('[fbgemm] quint8 tensor a+b=c:'...
